                <p>A bit (66) comprises a shank (176) extending along an axis (AX) between a proximal end (178) and a distal end (180), an interface (124) arranged between the proximal end (178) and the distal end (180), the interface (124) comprising at least two outermost drive portions (202) spaced from one another to define a maximum drive dimension of the interface (124) with the two outermost drive portions (202) each separately spaced at a first interface distance (204) from the axis (AX), and a resilient arm (188) extending from the proximal end (178) of the shank (176) to an arm end (200). The resilient arm (188) comprises an outer arm surface (222) facing away from the axis (AX), and a retention surface (224) facing toward the distal end (180) of the shank (176) and radially aligned about the axis (AX) with one of the outermost drive portions (202). The resilient arm (188) is movable relative to the axis (AX) between a first position where the outer arm surface (222) is spaced from the axis (AX) at a first arm distance (226) greater than the first interface distance (204), and a second position where the outer arm surface (222) is spaced from the axis (AX) at a second arm distance (228) less than the first arm distance (226) and less than or equal to the first interface distance (204).</p>
